# Units masked on vip, one per line. Mask, not disable: a disabled unit can still be started by a
# socket, a timer or a dependency. Units that do not exist on the board are skipped.
#
# vip's pedal root is built from packages (docs/vip-image.md), so most of piv's list (desktop,
# snapd, cloud-init, ModemManager, PipeWire) was never installed. What's left is maintenance that
# wakes up on its own: updates and checks happen when you choose, not mid-gig.
apt-daily.service
apt-daily.timer
apt-daily-upgrade.service
apt-daily-upgrade.timer
dpkg-db-backup.service
dpkg-db-backup.timer
e2scrub_all.service
e2scrub_all.timer
e2scrub_reap.service
fstrim.service
fstrim.timer
motd-news.service
motd-news.timer
# rpi-eeprom ships this and enables it: `rpi-eeprom-update -s -a` at every boot, which *applies* a
# pending bootloader update. The tooling is wanted (vcgencmd, rpi-eeprom-config); flashing the
# EEPROM is the owner's decision, made where the board can be reached, not a side effect of an
# image build.
rpi-eeprom-update.service
#
# Deliberately NOT masked:
#   systemd-timesyncd   vip has no RTC battery; without it the clock starts wherever it stopped.
#   systemd-networkd, wpa_supplicant@wlan0, systemd-resolved
#                       WiFi is the way in (no cable near vip).
